<span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Local Areas</span>
<h1>My Dinh by Motorbike: Motorbike Rental Planning in Hanoi</h1>
<p>My Dinh is Hanoi&rsquo;s modern quarter, the stadium-and-towers district out west in Nam Tu Liem where the city puts on its contemporary face, wide corridors, new blocks, convention halls and the capital&rsquo;s big-event venues, and for a rental rider it offers a base with a different arithmetic from the lakeside one, more room, calmer streets and a longer, more deliberate ride between home and the historic centre. Planning a stay here is planning that relationship honestly, the modern west as the living room, the old centre as the destination, and the machine as the bridge between the two. It suits riders who want space and quiet, and it rewards riders who plan.</p>
<p>The rental counter is at Motorbike Rental - Nguyen Tu, 112 Nguyen Van Cu in Long Bien, across the Red River on the city&rsquo;s eastern side, and the geography of that fact shapes every plan on this page. Start at the <a href="/motorbike-rental-hanoi-old-quarter/">Old Quarter motorbike rental</a> hub, see the machines and the verified prices at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> guide, browse the wider <a href="/motorbike-guides/">motorbike guides</a>, read the <a href="/motorbike-rental-hanoi-old-quarter/nam-tu-liem-rental-planning/">Nam Tu Liem rental planning</a> page for the district-level picture, and see the <a href="/motorbike-rental-hanoi-old-quarter/cau-giay-rental-planning/">Cau Giay rental planning</a> page for the neighbouring district on the centre run.</p>
<nav class="toc">
<ol>
